# Prime Linux release keys — ssh-keygen "allowed signers" format, one per line:
#   prime-release@prime-linux namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA… comment
#
# Every computer keeps the list it was installed with, and an update on the
# stable channel is only installed when its v* tag is signed by a key listed
# HERE, in the copy already on that computer (layer/bin/prime-release-verify).
# A new key therefore only arrives inside an update an existing key signed.
#
# Empty until the first release key is made (tools/release-sign.sh --new-key);
# while it is empty, updates are not signature-checked, and prime-update says so.
